  <reason>Subject and account: The subject of this report is Sana Aslam, holder of account PK**HABB****9538, opened on 27 April 2022. The customer's declared occupation is student, with a declared income of PKR 25,000 per month.

Activity summary: During the period 2 March 2026 to 10 March 2026, the account recorded 18 credits totalling PKR 1,060,000 as well as 4 debits totalling PKR 984,000. The credits arrived as 18 interbank (IBFT) transfers from 13 distinct senders. The activity was detected on 10 March 2026, when Tazama typology MULE-01 scored 360 against an alert threshold of 300.

Grounds for suspicion: The account received funds from 13 distinct senders within the activity window. Funds did not remain in the account: debits equal to 93% of credits, with a median of 1.5 hours between the latest credit and each debit. For a customer whose declared occupation is student, credits in the activity window were 42.4 times the declared monthly income, against a declared income of PKR 25,000 per month. A note by Fraud Desk (10 March 2026): "Two sender banks raised fraud recall requests against inbound transfers to this account, citing scam complaints." Taken together, these indicators are consistent with suspected money mule activity; the reporting entity has not established the underlying offence.

Flow of funds: Of the outgoing funds, PKR 516,000 was sent to QuickPay wallet ***0932 (WLT****0932, Synthetic EMI) in 2 transactions. Of the outgoing funds, PKR 468,000 was withdrawn as Cash (ATM) in 2 transactions.

Other considerations: Screening of the subject returned no match on sanctions, PEP or adverse-media screening on 29 March 2026.

Action taken by the reporting entity: Action taken: a note by L2 analyst (12 March 2026): "Outgoing wallet transfers placed on hold pending review. No contact made with the customer about this review."</reason>
